      "content": "{\"classifications\":{\"42\":\"1\",\"50\":\"0\",\"57\":\"1\",\"89\":\"1\",\"133\":\"0\",\"157\":\"0\",\"189\":\"0\",\"214\":\"0\",\"240\":\"0\",\"299\":\"1\",\"453\":\"0\",\"490\":\"0\",\"597\":\"0\",\"630\":\"0\",\"656\":\"0\",\"714\":\"1\",\"721\":\"0\",\"744\":\"0\",\"773\":\"1\",\"794\":\"1\",\"805\":\"0\",\"817\":\"0\",\"871\":\"0\",\"873\":\"1\",\"918\":\"0\",\"964\":\"0\",\"967\":\"0\",\"1021\":\"0\",\"1043\":\"1\",\"1060\":\"1\",\"1086\":\"0\",\"1118\":\"0\",\"1139\":\"0\",\"1155\":\"1\",\"1177\":\"0\",\"1230\":\"1\",\"1257\":\"1\",\"1313\":\"0\",\"1320\":\"1\",\"1325\":\"0\",\"1610\":\"0\",\"1736\":\"0\",\"1747\":\"1\",\"1749\":\"0\",\"1827\":\"1\",\"1862\":\"1\",\"1897\":\"0\",\"1927\":\"1\",\"1957\":\"0\",\"2003\":\"0\",\"2026\":\"1\",\"2143\":\"0\",\"2318\":\"1\",\"2335\":\"1\",\"2368\":\"1\",\"2382\":\"1\",\"2627\":\"1\",\"2675\":\"0\",\"2697\":\"1\",\"2807\":\"0\",\"2827\":\"0\",\"2869\":\"0\",\"2895\":\"1\",\"3038\":\"0\",\"3047\":\"1\",\"3143\":\"1\",\"3149\":\"1\",\"3201\":\"1\",\"3252\":\"1\",\"3271\":\"1\",\"3477\":\"0\",\"3482\":\"1\",\"3501\":\"0\",\"3534\":\"0\",\"3560\":\"0\",\"3577\":\"0\",\"3659\":\"0\",\"3687\":\"0\",\"3729\":\"1\",\"3744\":\"1\",\"3817\":\"0\",\"3845\":\"0\",\"3914\":\"1\",\"3950\":\"0\",\"4022\":\"0\",\"4122\":\"1\",\"4124\":\"0\",\"4184\":\"0\",\"4207\":\"0\",\"4208\":\"0\",\"4295\":\"1\",\"4328\":\"1\",\"4344\":\"0\",\"4403\":\"0\",\"4508\":\"1\",\"4531\":\"0\",\"4585\":\"1\",\"4677\":\"0\",\"4771\":\"1\",\"4774\":\"1\"},\"codebook\":{\"definition\":\"Credit-claiming occurs when a senator presents themself, their legislative work, advocacy, influence, or congressional role as having produced or helped produce a concrete governmental action, benefit, resource, policy outcome, or recognition.\",\"clarification\":\"Classify a release as credit-claiming when it links the senator to an achievement or beneficial result. This includes statements that the senator secured funding, authored or passed a measure that yielded a benefit, successfully pressed an agency, helped obtain a designation or federal decision, or claims that prior legislative work produced a current outcome. Credit can be claimed individually or jointly with colleagues, a delegation, or a party. A bill's passage or committee approval can qualify when the senator highlights their authorship, sponsorship, amendment, or other substantive role in that achievement.\",\"positive_examples\":[{\"text\":\"Sen. Talent announced that USDA declared most of Missouri a disaster area and stated that he \\\"worked with USDA officials to expedite the approval\\\" of the Governor's request.\",\"explanation\":\"The release directly attributes a concrete federal disaster designation and resulting assistance eligibility to Talent's efforts to expedite approval.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Dorgan announced Bismarck State College's national designation and stated that he \\\"authored legislation, which was signed into law, that created the National Center designation.\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"Dorgan explicitly connects his authorship of enacted legislation to the beneficial designation received by an institution in his state.\"},{\"text\":\"Sens. Baucus and Tester stated they had \\\"delivered on their promise to secure federal funding\\\" for $12.5 million in military projects in Butte.\",\"explanation\":\"This is an explicit claim of responsibility for obtaining specific federal funds for a local community.\"}],\"negative_clarification\":\"Do not classify releases as credit-claiming when they merely state a policy view, criticize an administration or other officials, announce an agency action without connecting it to the senator's efforts, commemorate a person or event, invite constituents to an event, or express support for or opposition to pending legislation. Introducing, cosponsoring, or voting for a bill without an asserted accomplishment or result is generally treated as position-taking rather than credit-claiming.\",\"negative_examples\":[{\"text\":\"Sen. Kerry criticized the Dubai Ports deal as a \\\"mismanaged and misguided debacle\\\" and called for congressional review.\",\"explanation\":\"The statement criticizes the Administration's actions but does not claim that Kerry obtained a benefit or produced a governmental outcome.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Allard invited residents to attend a Greeley town meeting to discuss issues important to them.\",\"explanation\":\"This is constituent outreach, with no claimed policy achievement, resource delivery, or successful intervention.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Salazar announced that he joined colleagues in supporting a White House compromise on the PATRIOT Act.\",\"explanation\":\"The release conveys support for a compromise but does not claim that Salazar secured, enacted, or otherwise produced the outcome.\"}]}}",
